mixin () {
  public query func getApiDoc() : async Text {
    let lines : [Text] = [
      "# Freelance ERP Consulting Backend API",
      "",
      "Backend for a single-consultant freelance ERP consulting business. It stores",
      "clients, engagements, and time entries, and derives profitability analytics",
      "(dashboard totals, per-client and per-engagement rankings, a 12-month trend,",
      "and an unbilled-work summary). All business data is private to the principal",
      "that created it.",
      "",
      "## Authentication",
      "",
      "Every data endpoint requires a signed (non-anonymous) caller. Anonymous callers",
      "are rejected with a trap whose message is `Sign-in required` on all client,",
      "engagement, time-entry, analytics, and seed endpoints.",
      "",
      "The frontend signs in through Internet Identity and pins a derivation origin,",
      "published at `/.well-known/ii-derivation-origin` when available. An agent that",
      "already holds the user's Internet Identity authorization derives the correct",
      "per-app principal against that origin (for example",
      "`icp identity link web <name> --app <host>`). Such a delegation acts with the",
      "user's full authority in this app until it expires.",
      "",
      "## Registration prerequisite",
      "",
      "Signing in is not the same as being registered. Registration happens only when",
      "a caller signs in through the app's own frontend, which calls",
      "`_initialize_access_control` (or `_internet_identity_sign_in_finish`) once. A",
      "principal that never did so is unregistered even if it belongs to the app's",
      "owner, and a signed-in caller derived against a different origin is a different",
      "principal than the one the frontend registered.",
      "",
      "- The first principal to call `_initialize_access_control` becomes `#admin`;",
      "  every later principal becomes `#user`.",
      "- `getCallerUserRole()` returns `#guest` for an anonymous caller and traps with",
      "  `User is not registered` for a signed-in but unregistered caller.",
      "- `isCallerAdmin()` traps with `User is not registered` for an unregistered",
      "  signed-in caller.",
      "- `assignCallerUserRole(user, role)` traps with",
      "  `Unauthorized: Only admins can assign user roles` unless the caller is an",
      "  admin.",
      "",
      "The business endpoints (clients, engagements, time entries, analytics, seed)",
      "do not consult the role table; they only require a non-anonymous caller and",
      "scope every read and write to that caller's principal. A direct API caller",
      "should call `_initialize_access_control` once as a signed-in caller before any",
      "role-guarded call, including the guarded queries `getCallerUserRole` and",
      "`isCallerAdmin`.",
      "",
      "## Authorization and data scoping",
      "",
      "All business data is per-owner. Every record carries an `owner : Principal`",
      "field set to the creating caller. Reads return only records owned by the",
      "caller; updates and deletes on a record owned by another principal return",
      "`null` (for updates) or `false` (for deletes) rather than trapping. There is no",
      "cross-owner sharing.",
      "",
      "## Units and encodings",
      "",
      "- `Timestamp` is `Int`, milliseconds since the Unix epoch (UTC).",
      "- `ClientId`, `EngagementId`, and `TimeEntryId` are `Nat`, assigned",
      "  sequentially from a shared counter starting at 0.",
      "- `hours` is a whole number of hours (`Nat`).",
      "- Monetary values (`billableRate`, `costRate`, `fixedFee`, `expenseAmount`,",
      "  `revenue`, `cost`, `unbilledValue`) are `Nat` in whole currency units.",
      "- `margin` and `marginPercent` are `Int` (margin can be negative).",
      "- `endDate`, `fixedFee`, and `expenseAmount` are optional (`?T`); `null` means",
      "  not set.",
      "- `billingModel` is `#hourly` or `#fixedFee`. `status` variants are",
      "  `#lead`/`#active`/`#archived` for clients and",
      "  `#proposed`/`#active`/`#completed`/`#archived` for engagements.",
      "",
      "## Revenue and margin rules",
      "",
      "- Hourly engagements: revenue for a billable entry is `hours * billableRate`.",
      "- Fixed-fee engagements: the `fixedFee` is counted exactly once per engagement,",
      "  on the first billable entry encountered, across every aggregation path",
      "  (dashboard, per-client and per-engagement profitability, monthly trend, and",
      "  unbilled summary). Non-billable entries contribute no revenue.",
      "- Cost for an entry is `hours * costRate`, regardless of billing model.",
      "- `utilizationPercent` is `billableHours * 100 / totalHours`, or 0 when no",
      "  hours are logged.",
      "- `marginPercent` is `(revenue - cost) * 100 / revenue`, or 0 when revenue is 0.",
      "",
      "## Public methods",
      "",
      "Clients and engagements:",
      "- `listClients(filter)` / `getClient(id)` - query.",
      "- `createClient(input)` / `updateClient(id, input)` / `deleteClient(id)`.",
      "- `listEngagements(filter)` / `getEngagement(id)` - query.",
      "- `createEngagement(input)` / `updateEngagement(id, input)` /",
      "  `deleteEngagement(id)`.",
      "",
      "Time entries:",
      "- `listTimeEntries(filter)` / `getTimeEntry(id)` - query.",
      "- `createTimeEntry(input)` / `updateTimeEntry(id, input)` /",
      "  `deleteTimeEntry(id)`.",
      "- `setTimeEntryInvoiced(id, invoiced)` - marks a time entry invoiced or not.",
      "- `listWeekEntries(weekStart)` - query; entries on or after `weekStart`.",
      "",
      "Analytics (all query):",
      "- `getDashboardSummary()` - total revenue, total cost, gross margin, billable",
      "  hours, total hours, and utilization across all of the caller's engagements.",
      "- `getClientProfitability()` - per-client revenue, cost, margin, margin percent.",
      "- `getEngagementProfitability()` - per-engagement revenue, cost, margin, margin",
      "  percent.",
      "- `getMonthlyTrend(months)` - `months` calendar buckets ending with the current",
      "  month, oldest first; each point carries year, month, hours, and revenue.",
      "  Returns an empty array when `months` is 0.",
      "- `getUnbilledSummary()` - logged-but-not-invoiced billable hours, their value,",
      "  and the entry count.",
      "",
      "Seeding:",
      "- `seedSampleData()` - creates sample clients, engagements, and time entries",
      "  owned by the caller so the dashboard and analytics are populated on first",
      "  sign-in. It is additive: calling it again creates another full set of sample",
      "  records rather than replacing existing data.",
      "",
      "Access control:",
      "- `_initialize_access_control()` - registers the caller (first caller becomes",
      "  admin).",
      "- `_internet_identity_sign_in_start()` / `_internet_identity_sign_in_finish()`",
      "  - Internet Identity sign-in handshake.",
      "- `getCallerUserRole()` - query; the caller's role.",
      "- `isCallerAdmin()` - query; whether the caller is an admin.",
      "- `assignCallerUserRole(user, role)` - admin-only role assignment.",
      "",
      "## Lifecycle and polling",
      "",
      "All analytics endpoints are `query` calls and return a complete snapshot in one",
      "response; there is nothing to poll. After a mutation, re-issue the relevant",
      "query to observe the new state. `getMonthlyTrend` buckets by calendar month",
      "using the canister's current time, so the window shifts as time passes.",
      "",
      "## Mutation retry safety",
      "",
      "`createClient`, `createEngagement`, and `createTimeEntry` are not idempotent:",
      "each call allocates a new id and inserts a new record, so retrying a call that",
      "actually succeeded creates a duplicate. `updateClient`, `updateEngagement`,",
      "`updateTimeEntry`, and `setTimeEntryInvoiced` are idempotent for the same",
      "arguments. `deleteClient`, `deleteEngagement`, and `deleteTimeEntry` return",
      "`false` when the record is already gone, so a retry is safe. `seedSampleData`",
      "is additive and not idempotent.",
      "",
      "## Errors and gotchas",
      "",
      "- Anonymous callers trap with `Sign-in required` on every data endpoint.",
      "- Role-guarded calls trap with `User is not registered` for an unregistered",
      "  signed-in caller, and `Unauthorized: Only admins can assign user roles` for a",
      "  non-admin role assignment.",
      "- Update and delete on a record owned by another principal return `null` /",
      "  `false`; they do not trap.",
      "- `getClient`, `getEngagement`, and `getTimeEntry` return `null` for a missing",
      "  or non-owned id.",
      "- `getMonthlyTrend(0)` returns an empty array.",
      "- The OQL `schema()` / `execute()` endpoints expose the `client`, `engagement`,",
      "  and `timeEntry` entities to the Data Intelligence agent, scoped to the",
      "  caller's own records.",
    ];
    lines.values().join("\n");
  };
};
